  "term": "cerebral infarction",
  "definition": "Cerebral infarction is an area of brain tissue death in the cerebrum caused by too little arterial or venous blood flow. It is commonly described by which side or lobe of the cerebrum is affected, the blood vessel territory involved, or the underlying cause.",
